</form><html xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xmlns:math="java.lang.Math" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xs="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" xmlns:fo="http://www.w3.org/1999/XSL/Format" xmlns:fn="http://www.w3.org/2005/02/xpath-functions" xmlns:xdt="http://www.w3.org/2005/02/xpath-datatypes" xmlns:caml="http://lc.ca.gov/legalservices/schemas/caml.1#" xmlns:xhtml="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><head><title>HR139:v99#DOCUMENT</title><meta name="dc:identifier" content="HR139"/><meta name="dc:title" content="HR &#xA;              139-&#xA;                INTRODUCED&#xA;              "/><meta http-equiv="Content-Type" content="text/html;charset=utf-8"/></head><body><span class="hidden"><h2>Bill Start</h2></span><div id="bill_all" align="justify"><div id="about"><br clear="all"/><div align="center"><table style="border-collapse: collapse" cellSpacing="0" align="center" role="presentation"><tbody><tr><td align="center"/></tr></tbody></table></div><br clear="all"/><div align="center"><font size="3" style="FONT-FAMILY: MinionPC, Arial Unicode MS">
                    CALIFORNIA LEGISLATURE—
                    2025–2026 REGULAR SESSION</font></div><br clear="all"/><span id="bill_house_num"><div style="float: left; width:50%; font-weight: bold; "><span style="text-transform: uppercase; text-align:left;width:50%;"><b>
                House Resolution
              </b></span></div><div style="float:right; width:50%; text-align:right;"><span style="text-transform: uppercase;"><b>No. 139</b></span></div></span><hr/><br clear="all"/><div align="center"><table style="border-collapse: collapse" cellSpacing="0" align="center" role="presentation"><tbody><tr><td id="bill_authors" align="center"><span style="font-weight:bold;">Introduced by Assembly Member Hoover<br/></span></td></tr><tr><td id="bill_intro_date" align="center" class="textcenter"><br/>August 18, 2026</td></tr></tbody></table></div><hr/><br clear="all"/><div id="title"><span style="font-weight:normal;font-size:0.9em;"> Relative to Lunar Landing Day. </span></div><br clear="all"/><br clear="all"/><div align="center"><h2>LEGISLATIVE COUNSEL'S DIGEST</h2></div><br/><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0"><span id="subject">HR 139, as introduced, Hoover.
                          </span></div><div><span id="digesttext"/></div><span class="hidden"><h2>Digest Key</h2></span></div><hr/><span class="hidden"><h2>Bill Text</h2></span><span class="Resolution" title="source: /caml:MeasureDoc/caml:Resolution&#xA;    "><span class="Whereas" id="id_C68B85E7-8867-4AEA-85FE-FF66A50E47A8"><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;">WHEREAS, On July 20, 1969, American Astronauts Neil Armstrong and Buzz Aldrin landed the Lunar Module “Eagle” on the Moon while Michael Collins orbited the Moon in the Command Module Columbia, collectively known as the Apollo 11 mission, conducted by the National Aeronautics and Space Administration, resulting in the first humans landing on another celestial body; and</div></span><span class="Whereas" id="id_D9BF04A5-B481-468A-8330-4343E56BD742"><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;">WHEREAS, The Apollo 11 lunar landing was one of the most important events in the history of humankind, requiring the efforts of over 410,000 people working in concert; and</div></span><span class="Whereas" id="id_91D3D1C1-6A97-466C-A863-315A77248F5F"><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;">WHEREAS, The contributions of the engineers and machinists working at related companies in California led to the design and successful use of the engines used to power the rocket for the Apollo 11 mission; and</div></span><span class="Whereas" id="id_100AE2D2-7994-4ECD-A6B5-B8BFBD617F74"><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;">WHEREAS, The Apollo 11 mission effectively ended the Space Race and fulfilled a national goal proposed in 1961 by President John F. Kennedy: “before this decade is out, of landing a man on the Moon and returning him safely to the Earth”; and</div></span><span class="Whereas" id="id_769A1920-B96A-41B9-AB9C-0D62490F6DCA"><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;">WHEREAS, For over 70 years, the North American Rockwell company site in Downey, California produced and tested many of the 20th century’s greatest aviation, missile, and space endeavors; and</div></span><span class="Whereas" id="id_89404D22-735C-4303-B8BA-3EFA48DD3D05"><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;">WHEREAS, Rocket engines used in the Apollo missions were designed, manufactured, and tested at the Aerojet company site in Rancho Cordova, California; and</div></span><span class="Whereas" id="id_DC17E7BC-1181-4E77-9FCD-AFBFF8B98882"><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;">WHEREAS, The lunar landing was witnessed by the largest simultaneous viewing audience in television broadcast history, and was publicized in every major language on Earth by newspapers, radio stations, and international broadcast networks; and</div></span><span class="Whereas" id="id_FDC58F25-A675-4D1C-AD77-5CE4A0C13BB2"><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;">WHEREAS, The Apollo missions enabled people of the world to view their planet Earth in a new way when for the first time, humans saw the entire planet from afar, a tiny, lovely, fragile “blue marble” hanging in the blackness of space; and</div></span><span class="Whereas" id="id_C7AA9F4F-B85F-4FC6-81D0-6B25E098DA25"><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;">WHEREAS, Science, technology, engineering, and math (STEM) education in the United States is lagging behind that of other nations, and the promotion of science and space exploration can lead to an improvement in STEM education for current students and the next generation of explorers, engineers, artists, and creators; now, therefore, be it</div></span><span class="Resolved" id="id_8B1B7827-2DB9-4005-8196-6269CE0199DA"><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;">Resolved by the Assembly of the State of California, That the Assembly establishes July 20, 2026, and every July 20 thereafter, as Lunar Landing Day in the State of California; and be it further</div></span><span class="Resolved" id="id_7979B399-6D8A-40CA-9789-964C54CE9A09"><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;">Resolved, That the Assembly encourages people throughout California to celebrate Lunar Landing Day by doing all of the following:</div><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;">(1) Honoring the contributions of the aerospace engineers in this state who contributed to the success of the Apollo 11 mission;</div><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;">(2) Honoring all who study, design, fabricate, and construct the technologies and applications that allow human space exploration and research;</div><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;">(3) Educating family, friends, and all others about its value and the impact of human space exploration on the economy, national security, society, and human health.</div><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;">(4) Inspiring students to pursue STEM education and seize the
		  opportunity to amplify the United States’ tradition of discovery and innovation; and</div><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;">(5) Celebrating the accomplishments of the United States in science and space exploration and research in the past, and promoting the achievements yet to come in the future; and be it further</div></span><span class="Resolved" id="id_646C75C8-EE55-4F52-8032-42E64F92B44B"><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;">Resolved, That the Chief Clerk of the Assembly transmit copies of this resolution to the author for appropriate distribution.</div></span></span></div></body></html>
